From 2b59bd1a8b6b24d6046201107b9bbd48702061f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergio Gonzalez Martin <sergiog@microsoft.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 22:26:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Recover malformed baseline Huffman scans

Backport the remaining Rust-source delta from zune-image PR518:
https://github.com/etemesi254/zune-image/pull/518
Upstream head: 52376a5ae851b0bff9b7934a1e4ceb8ed5329b0c
Upstream base: 2cdbbf554e7da373d3418ab327a0db7c4abb50cd
Apply after PR516 and PR534, preserving PR525/PR526 optimizations.

Recover invalid baseline Huffman codes in permissive mode by consuming
17 bits and substituting zero. Preserve predictors and decoded AC values,
finish partial MCUs and reconstruct missing MCUs as neutral coefficients.
Keep real buffered entropy distinct from a prefetched EOI marker and
bound reconstruction work for the remaining image.

Keep unknown entropy markers fatal before EOF conversion or permissive
partial-success recovery, including incremental decoding. Preserve the
malformed smoke fixture as a fatal-error regression.

Use the existing generic box reconstruction when visible chroma width
is one or two samples. Calculate visible width with ceiling division,
not the padded MCU stride, and retain configured row dispatch.

Retain progressive error/publication policy, corruption tracking,
suspending refill, widened coefficients and scaled output. Integrate
empty-restart lookahead in the existing refill helper. Embed authored
controls so the recovery unit tests are self-contained. Count reconstructed
IDCT blocks, including PR526's inline DC-only path, without replacing
configured dispatch.

PR518's color precision changes are already covered by PR499.
Do not duplicate them or import unrelated upstream-base changes.
